1
00:00:00,034 --> 00:00:01,135
Are you serious, Lando?

2
00:00:01,135 --> 00:00:02,436
You brought a typewriter here?

3
00:00:02,436 --> 00:00:05,306
Do you know that this typewriter is magical?

4
00:00:05,306 --> 00:00:08,676
This thing can change your life.

5
00:00:08,676 --> 00:00:13,047
I trusted you, but you're a traitor!

6
00:00:13,047 --> 00:00:14,433
Go ahead, kill me!

7
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:16,417
I'm not scared to die!

8
00:00:16,417 --> 00:00:18,419
I won't let my dad kill you.

9
00:00:18,419 --> 00:00:19,820
I will take the bullet for you.

10
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,121
We'll be together.

11
00:00:21,121 --> 00:00:22,423
This is what I want.

12
00:00:22,423 --> 00:00:23,857
This is my wish.

13
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:26,727
I just want to make sure
my loved ones are safe.

14
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:27,928
Aunt Tess is safe.

15
00:00:27,928 --> 00:00:30,097
- And Joyce, too.
- Dex!

16
00:00:30,097 --> 00:00:31,432
Liam is my husband.

17
00:00:31,432 --> 00:00:33,434
It's not enough that
I bring you back to life, Liam.

18
00:00:33,434 --> 00:00:37,538
I can find a way to remove Joyce
from your life.

19
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:39,081
Via.

20
00:00:52,086 --> 00:00:54,688
<i>Forgive me, Sabel.</i>

21
00:00:54,688 --> 00:00:56,457
<i>I was blinded.</i>

22
00:00:56,457 --> 00:00:59,692
<i>I was blinded by my love for you.</i>

23
00:01:00,794 --> 00:01:04,497
<i>I don't know if I can call it love.</i>

24
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:07,311
<i>If only I could turn back time,</i>

25
00:01:07,311 --> 00:01:10,135
<i>I wouldn't even try
to separate the two of you.</i>

26
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:12,906
<i>Sabel...</i>

27
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:14,641
<i>Diego...</i>

28
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:16,910
<i>Forgive me.</i>

29
00:01:17,945 --> 00:01:20,647
<i>Maybe this is my curse.</i>

30
00:01:20,647 --> 00:01:26,265
<i>I'm the only one
who can't use this typewriter.</i>

31
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:32,725
<i>I'm the only one who can't turn back time
to correct my mistakes.</i>

32
00:01:58,752 --> 00:02:04,292
Hans, I don't blame Liam
for turning himself in.

33
00:02:05,692 --> 00:02:10,430
I wish I knew where he is.

34
00:02:15,803 --> 00:02:22,346
Joyce, I know you love Liam.

35
00:02:24,479 --> 00:02:26,251
But...

36
00:02:27,614 --> 00:02:30,924
while I'm here...

37
00:02:32,453 --> 00:02:35,408
I hope I'll be enough to make you feel safe.

38
00:02:36,346 --> 00:02:38,580
I'm sorry, Hans.

39
00:02:40,194 --> 00:02:41,830
Sorry.

40
00:02:44,131 --> 00:02:47,300
I know why it is Liam.

41
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:53,139
Not because you're lacking.

42
00:02:56,877 --> 00:02:59,316
But because...

43
00:03:01,315 --> 00:03:04,339
I have loved Liam ever since.

44
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:10,331
What do you mean, Joyce?

45
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:15,675
You've been with Liam before we got together?

46
00:03:23,437 --> 00:03:25,245
Hans, I'm sorry.

47
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:29,710
I need to know where Liam is.

48
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:32,458
I need your help.

49
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:38,632
Please.

50
00:04:05,979 --> 00:04:08,327
<i>I'm sorry, Hans.</i>

51
00:04:09,217 --> 00:04:13,108
<i>But I feel like there's something
you're not telling me.</i>

52
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:30,130
What are you doing?

53
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:32,232
Miss, it's just me.

54
00:05:32,232 --> 00:05:33,834
You don't need to pretend.

55
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:36,627
I even changed my outfit so it'd be safe.

56
00:05:37,871 --> 00:05:41,174
I'm just pretending to be a cripple.

57
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:47,672
But my wound and stitches really hurt.

58
00:05:49,316 --> 00:05:51,852
What are you doing here?

59
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:52,919
So cranky.

60
00:05:52,919 --> 00:05:56,189
Didn't I tell you to notify me first?

61
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:58,552
What if Liam sees you?

62
00:05:59,526 --> 00:06:02,729
You're so cranky. Where's Sir Liam?

63
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:05,198
He went out to buy medicine.

64
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:08,435
He'll be back anytime soon, Queenie.

65
00:06:08,435 --> 00:06:10,270
Where? In town?

66
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:12,645
It will take him a while, for sure.

67
00:06:15,042 --> 00:06:18,411
I got you your favorites.

68
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,948
Wine.

69
00:06:21,948 --> 00:06:23,884
Right? I told you.

70
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,818
You just lack faith in me.

71
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,622
With this, here.

72
00:06:28,622 --> 00:06:30,223
See?

73
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:32,658
Let's have some wine.

74
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:35,658
Here.

75
00:06:38,614 --> 00:06:41,250
Here's the cash you asked me to withdraw.

76
00:06:42,536 --> 00:06:44,286
See?

77
00:06:48,894 --> 00:06:50,477
So...

78
00:06:50,477 --> 00:06:52,728
don't you have any plans of going home?

79
00:06:55,128 --> 00:06:58,376
I'm only starting to get Liam's trust.

80
00:07:01,455 --> 00:07:03,861
- More.
- Okay.

81
00:07:29,209 --> 00:07:31,137
I missed this.

82
00:07:36,768 --> 00:07:38,270
Via?

83
00:07:43,381 --> 00:07:44,903
Hans?

84
00:07:48,434 --> 00:07:50,236
What are you doing here?

85
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:52,839
What if someone's following you?

86
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:54,941
Why?

87
00:07:54,941 --> 00:07:57,543
Are you surprised to see me?

88
00:07:57,543 --> 00:07:59,712
Are you scared that Ramon will find you?

89
00:07:59,712 --> 00:08:01,722
What have you been doing?

90
00:08:02,582 --> 00:08:05,184
After you exposed everything, Liam...

91
00:08:05,184 --> 00:08:09,388
you even got your family involved,
and Joyce, and her family.

92
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:11,737
You'll just hide here?

93
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,928
Liam, why...

94
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:17,196
Why did Joyce choose you?

95
00:08:17,196 --> 00:08:20,266
- You're a coward.
- Hans, you don't understand.

96
00:08:20,266 --> 00:08:24,570
I just need to take care of Via first.
Then I'll go back to Joyce.

97
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:26,405
Take care of Via?
What are you talking about?

98
00:08:26,405 --> 00:08:28,584
What kind of excuse is that, Liam?

99
00:08:30,042 --> 00:08:32,411
I can understand if you and Via
are on the brink of death,

100
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:33,579
but it looks like...

101
00:08:33,579 --> 00:08:35,780
Look at your situation.

102
00:08:36,571 --> 00:08:39,473
It seems like you're playing house!

103
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:50,646
Wait until I tell Joyce about
what you've been doing with Via.

104
00:08:51,485 --> 00:08:54,037
I'm done with your excuses, Liam.

105
00:08:56,216 --> 00:08:58,490
You've fooled everyone.

106
00:08:59,939 --> 00:09:01,997
Is that really your reason?

107
00:09:03,109 --> 00:09:04,528
Is that it?

108
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:07,647
Or do you have an agenda?

109
00:09:07,647 --> 00:09:09,782
You're a jerk.

110
00:09:11,183 --> 00:09:14,386
What? What are you saying?

111
00:09:15,121 --> 00:09:16,756
Oh no!

112
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:18,157
That's Attorney Hans.

113
00:09:18,157 --> 00:09:20,258
What is he doing here?

114
00:09:35,141 --> 00:09:37,143
Mister, I'm getting off here.

115
00:09:37,143 --> 00:09:40,012
Thank you so much for giving me a ride.

116
00:09:40,012 --> 00:09:44,884
I'm sorry, it took us a whole day
for this trip.

117
00:09:44,884 --> 00:09:46,352
Here's my payment.

118
00:09:46,352 --> 00:09:48,154
It's all yours.
You don't have to give me change.

119
00:09:48,154 --> 00:09:50,164
Thank you so much.

120
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:52,969
Be safe.

121
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:02,234
I gave way, but you're telling me I'm wrong!

122
00:10:02,234 --> 00:10:04,203
- You really didn't give way!
- Yet I'm still the bad guy?

123
00:10:04,203 --> 00:10:07,340
The truth is, you're waiting for me to fail!

124
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:09,809
I can't go downstairs.

125
00:10:09,809 --> 00:10:13,412
Attorney Hans is already
killing your boyfriend, Miss.

126
00:10:13,412 --> 00:10:14,914
Are you still going
to pretend that you can't walk?

127
00:10:14,914 --> 00:10:17,903
Come on, Queenie!

128
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:36,002
- Make no mistake!
- Attorney!

129
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,603
Sir Liam, that's enough.

130
00:10:37,603 --> 00:10:38,938
Liam, that's enough.

131
00:10:38,938 --> 00:10:40,680
Stop!

132
00:10:42,274 --> 00:10:44,076
Hey! Hey, stop!

133
00:10:44,076 --> 00:10:46,704
Stop, stop, stop!

134
00:10:47,511 --> 00:10:48,878
Via.

135
00:10:50,549 --> 00:10:52,305
You can walk?

136
00:10:55,454 --> 00:10:57,757
Love, I can explain.

137
00:10:57,757 --> 00:10:59,358
- Love...
- Via, you fooled me.

138
00:10:59,358 --> 00:11:00,893
No.

139
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:02,228
No.

140
00:11:02,228 --> 00:11:03,629
Come on.

141
00:11:03,629 --> 00:11:07,400
Hear me out. Just let me explain first, okay?

142
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,858
Liam.

143
00:11:12,738 --> 00:11:14,187
Joyce?

144
00:11:16,075 --> 00:11:17,422
Joyce.

145
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,750
Joyce.

146
00:11:43,305 --> 00:11:45,891
I want to get mad at you.

147
00:11:47,557 --> 00:11:51,821
I want to get mad about
all the mistakes you made.

148
00:11:55,281 --> 00:11:58,555
In this world and in our past life.

149
00:12:00,019 --> 00:12:02,157
Do you believe me now?

150
00:12:06,258 --> 00:12:08,422
I do, Liam.

151
00:12:14,133 --> 00:12:17,852
I believe you, but I hate you.

152
00:12:19,772 --> 00:12:23,691
I want to ask how you could do that?

153
00:12:26,011 --> 00:12:30,816
Why did you choose to lose your son and me?

154
00:12:30,816 --> 00:12:34,191
Joyce, forgive me.

155
00:12:35,821 --> 00:12:37,839
I was a coward.

156
00:12:39,992 --> 00:12:42,567
I forgot to fight.

157
00:12:45,064 --> 00:12:48,000
Forgive me because...

158
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,781
I became selfish.

159
00:12:52,471 --> 00:12:55,230
I thought you would be happy.

160
00:12:57,510 --> 00:12:59,763
But I was wrong, Joyce.

161
00:13:01,747 --> 00:13:05,261
I regret it so much because I know

162
00:13:05,261 --> 00:13:08,045
that I will pay for this my whole life.

163
00:13:09,318 --> 00:13:11,803
I know in my heart...

164
00:13:15,481 --> 00:13:22,010
that I will forgive you a hundred times over.

165
00:13:24,338 --> 00:13:25,994
Let's go home.

166
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,486
Come on, let's go home.

167
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:42,054
No! No!

168
00:13:42,054 --> 00:13:42,855
- No!
- Via...

169
00:13:42,855 --> 00:13:45,124
You're not going anywhere, Liam!
You're not leaving.

170
00:13:45,124 --> 00:13:46,725
He's not leaving.

171
00:13:46,725 --> 00:13:47,947
No.

172
00:13:48,812 --> 00:13:50,791
Via, that's enough.

173
00:13:52,690 --> 00:13:57,775
Don't trap yourself in the illusion of love
you're trying to believe in.

174
00:13:59,205 --> 00:14:02,057
Save some for yourself.

175
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:07,581
You have the guts to say that
because he chose you!

176
00:14:09,816 --> 00:14:13,519
You will never understand me, Joyce!

177
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:18,490
You don't know how it feels!

178
00:14:18,490 --> 00:14:20,025
You have no idea!

179
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,721
You don't know.

180
00:14:22,582 --> 00:14:25,158
Via, as women,

181
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:31,638
we should not let our world
revolve around a man.

182
00:14:32,973 --> 00:14:36,236
Via, we don't beg for love.

183
00:14:37,444 --> 00:14:39,494
Love shouldn't be forced.

184
00:14:42,716 --> 00:14:48,121
I hope you understand that
real love knows how to sacrifice...

185
00:14:48,121 --> 00:14:49,422
How to set things free.

186
00:14:49,422 --> 00:14:52,926
If that's the case, then set Liam free!

187
00:14:52,926 --> 00:14:54,394
Via!

188
00:14:56,872 --> 00:14:58,400
That's enough.

189
00:14:59,351 --> 00:15:01,000
Let them be happy.

190
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,408
No...

191
00:15:02,408 --> 00:15:04,271
No!

192
00:15:04,271 --> 00:15:06,744
You're not leaving, Liam.

193
00:15:07,674 --> 00:15:09,309
Liam, please.

194
00:15:09,309 --> 00:15:10,947
Please.

195
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:16,448
<i>I won't let my dad kill you.</i>

196
00:15:16,448 --> 00:15:19,345
<i>I will take the bullet for you.</i>

197
00:15:21,087 --> 00:15:22,489
<i>This is what I want.</i>

198
00:15:22,489 --> 00:15:24,244
<i>This is my wish.</i>

199
00:15:27,694 --> 00:15:30,430
Did you use the typewriter?

200
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,798
Via...

201
00:15:31,798 --> 00:15:33,099
Via, it always comes with a price.

202
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:35,802
I don't care, Liam!

203
00:15:35,802 --> 00:15:37,504
I can't bear losing you.

204
00:15:37,504 --> 00:15:39,272
I can't bear it.

205
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:40,173
I can't bear it.

206
00:15:40,173 --> 00:15:42,812
- I don't care what the price is.
- Via...

207
00:15:42,812 --> 00:15:44,310
Via!

208
00:15:47,814 --> 00:15:49,419
Via, please stop.

209
00:15:50,217 --> 00:15:52,018
That's enough. Stop.

210
00:15:52,018 --> 00:15:53,353
Liam, please.

211
00:15:53,353 --> 00:15:56,568
- Stop. That's enough...
- Please, please, please.

212
00:15:57,858 --> 00:15:59,526
Via.

213
00:15:59,526 --> 00:16:02,377
Think about it carefully.

214
00:16:06,199 --> 00:16:07,572
Sorry.

215
00:16:11,993 --> 00:16:13,423
Via.

216
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:19,166
Via, listen to me.

217
00:16:21,648 --> 00:16:23,783
Just this once,

218
00:16:26,943 --> 00:16:29,642
love yourself.

219
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:43,202
Let go of me!

220
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,628
Let's go.

221
00:16:46,539 --> 00:16:48,300
Liam, Joyce.

222
00:16:50,243 --> 00:16:52,597
I made a promise to your family.

223
00:17:58,878 --> 00:17:59,980
What's that?

224
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:01,289
What's that?

225
00:18:01,289 --> 00:18:03,024
Go hide.

226
00:18:03,024 --> 00:18:04,951
Hide. Stay there!

227
00:18:04,951 --> 00:18:05,986
- Don't...
- Edmond!

228
00:18:05,986 --> 00:18:08,320
Stay there!

229
00:18:34,247 --> 00:18:36,416
Edmond, stay here...

230
00:18:36,416 --> 00:18:39,119
Madam, I don't want to die yet.

231
00:18:39,119 --> 00:18:41,388
What's going on?

232
00:18:41,388 --> 00:18:43,723
I'm moving.

233
00:18:43,723 --> 00:18:45,315
Who is it?

234
00:18:46,713 --> 00:18:48,751
Who's there?

235
00:18:50,764 --> 00:18:53,166
- Who are you?
- Oh...

236
00:18:53,166 --> 00:18:56,440
What a lovely night for a reunion.

237
00:18:57,270 --> 00:18:59,471
Ramon dela Peña?

238
00:19:13,754 --> 00:19:14,988
Who are you?

239
00:19:14,988 --> 00:19:16,589
Go inside.

240
00:19:16,589 --> 00:19:17,905
Joyce...

241
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,956
Leave my family alone!

242
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:44,884
Edmond!

243
00:19:44,884 --> 00:19:45,985
You're a demon!

244
00:19:45,985 --> 00:19:47,554
Edmond!

245
00:19:47,554 --> 00:19:49,956
Demon!

246
00:19:49,956 --> 00:19:51,057
Don't touch me!

247
00:19:51,057 --> 00:19:53,067
Edmond, Edmond...

248
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:55,605
Why is this happening?

249
00:19:57,197 --> 00:19:58,832
What's going on here?

250
00:19:58,832 --> 00:20:00,066
- Mom!
- Liam, my son!

251
00:20:00,066 --> 00:20:02,768
- Mom, Mom.
- Dad!

252
00:20:04,003 --> 00:20:05,572
You took so long!

253
00:20:05,572 --> 00:20:06,906
Dad...

254
00:20:06,906 --> 00:20:08,174
Stay away from me!

255
00:20:08,174 --> 00:20:09,576
You're so evil!

256
00:20:09,576 --> 00:20:11,456
Where's my daughter?

257
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:14,080
She's alive.

258
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,982
So I'm begging you, Ramon.

259
00:20:15,982 --> 00:20:18,151
Stop this!

260
00:20:18,151 --> 00:20:20,144
It's not too late!

261
00:20:24,269 --> 00:20:26,814
It's really not too late.

262
00:20:28,094 --> 00:20:29,762
Okay?

263
00:20:29,762 --> 00:20:31,931
You're still alive.

264
00:20:31,931 --> 00:20:37,237
This is your chance to retract...

265
00:20:37,237 --> 00:20:41,674
every lie you said against me!

266
00:20:41,674 --> 00:20:42,969
Okay?

267
00:20:52,552 --> 00:20:56,789
You will admit that you're the mastermind.

268
00:20:56,789 --> 00:21:01,895
You killed Lando, and you shot Via.

269
00:21:01,895 --> 00:21:04,364
You really are crazy, aren't you?

270
00:21:04,364 --> 00:21:07,100
I won't commit any more sins!

271
00:21:08,829 --> 00:21:10,241
Why?

272
00:21:11,538 --> 00:21:14,160
If they all die...

273
00:21:15,909 --> 00:21:20,891
wouldn't it be your fault
because you didn't do as I say?

274
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:24,584
Don't! Don't! Don't!

275
00:21:24,584 --> 00:21:25,652
Don't...

276
00:21:25,652 --> 00:21:27,487
- Answer me!
- Don't...

277
00:21:27,487 --> 00:21:29,322
Don't...

278
00:21:29,322 --> 00:21:30,814
Don't...

279
00:21:38,565 --> 00:21:42,068
Oh my God, Miss Via. What happened here?

280
00:21:42,068 --> 00:21:44,237
I still want to become
Escale's editor-in-chief.

281
00:21:44,237 --> 00:21:46,243
Shut up, Queenie.

282
00:22:04,791 --> 00:22:06,717
What happened here?

283
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:09,420
Who are you?

284
00:22:10,330 --> 00:22:11,831
What will you do with a typewriter?

285
00:22:11,831 --> 00:22:12,832
Get that.

286
00:22:12,832 --> 00:22:14,678
Just get that.

287
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:17,983
Did you get hit
in the back or in the head?

288
00:22:22,008 --> 00:22:24,244
- Don't!
- Ramon!

289
00:22:24,244 --> 00:22:25,411
Kill me instead.

290
00:22:25,411 --> 00:22:27,046
Go on.

291
00:22:27,046 --> 00:22:28,715
Go on and kill me!

292
00:22:28,715 --> 00:22:30,883
For this to end!

293
00:22:30,883 --> 00:22:33,353
I'm the one who did you wrong! Kill me!

294
00:22:33,353 --> 00:22:35,654
Don't get them involved!

295
00:22:45,198 --> 00:22:50,436
You can't tell me what to do.

296
00:22:50,436 --> 00:22:51,938
Okay?

297
00:22:51,938 --> 00:22:55,205
You've been fooling me, Liam.

298
00:22:56,209 --> 00:23:01,374
Death is not enough

299
00:23:01,374 --> 00:23:06,429
for all the betrayal and hurt
you did to my daughter and me.

300
00:23:07,887 --> 00:23:10,089
How can I be sure they're safe?

301
00:23:10,089 --> 00:23:12,161
That you'll keep them out of this?

302
00:23:17,130 --> 00:23:19,799
You won't know.

303
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:23,119
You have no choice but to do as I say.

304
00:23:24,137 --> 00:23:26,864
Are you just going to use me
to clean your name?

305
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:30,677
I will do it.

306
00:23:30,677 --> 00:23:33,216
But don't ever get them involved.

307
00:23:38,372 --> 00:23:40,518
No one will get involved...

308
00:23:41,954 --> 00:23:44,904
if you do what I say.

309
00:23:53,966 --> 00:23:59,706
Just remember how you became
my puppet before.

310
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:12,352
Hi, baby boy.

311
00:24:12,352 --> 00:24:16,889
You know, for some reason,
my boss needs that typewriter.

312
00:24:16,889 --> 00:24:19,359
I'll just buy it from you.

313
00:24:19,359 --> 00:24:21,227
I don't want to fight, you know.

314
00:24:21,227 --> 00:24:23,496
It's not my brand.

315
00:24:23,496 --> 00:24:26,999
I'm good at lip-sync, but...

316
00:24:26,999 --> 00:24:28,634
Just give it to me
if you don't want to get hurt.

317
00:24:28,634 --> 00:24:30,236
No!

318
00:24:30,236 --> 00:24:31,835
- Give it to me.
- No.

319
00:24:31,835 --> 00:24:33,239
- Give it to me.
- No!

320
00:24:33,239 --> 00:24:34,841
- Give it to me!
- No!

321
00:24:34,841 --> 00:24:36,042
- Give it to me!
- Stop!

322
00:24:36,042 --> 00:24:37,844
- No!
- Give it to me!

323
00:24:37,844 --> 00:24:38,745
- This is mine!
- Stop!

324
00:24:38,745 --> 00:24:39,879
- This is mine!
- Let me have it!

325
00:24:39,879 --> 00:24:42,882
This is mine! Let go...

326
00:24:42,882 --> 00:24:44,050
Give it to me!

327
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,885
Give it to me!

328
00:24:45,885 --> 00:24:47,658
Watch over him.

329
00:24:48,988 --> 00:24:50,556
My baby...

330
00:24:50,556 --> 00:24:52,041
Sorry.

331
00:24:53,611 --> 00:24:55,236
Dad!

332
00:24:56,863 --> 00:24:59,103
Stop this!

333
00:25:00,150 --> 00:25:02,568
There's still another way.

334
00:25:02,568 --> 00:25:03,936
Here's the typewriter, Dad!

335
00:25:03,936 --> 00:25:05,838
- Here it is!
- You again?

336
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:09,442
I got the typewriter!

337
00:25:09,442 --> 00:25:12,378
Dad, this has powers!

338
00:25:12,378 --> 00:25:15,214
This can change everything.

339
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:16,949
Everything.

340
00:25:16,949 --> 00:25:20,620
Everything in the past can change.

341
00:25:20,620 --> 00:25:23,080
We can be complete again.

342
00:25:24,838 --> 00:25:28,715
You've gone crazy like your mom!

343
00:25:29,962 --> 00:25:31,504
Hans, now!

344
00:25:32,366 --> 00:25:33,766
Dad!

345
00:25:34,434 --> 00:25:35,824
Dad!

346
00:25:39,439 --> 00:25:41,319
Dad, go on. Run! Call the police. Dad, go on!

347
00:25:41,319 --> 00:25:43,442
Help them escape!

348
00:25:43,442 --> 00:25:46,029
- Dad!
- My God, Danilo!

349
00:25:55,066 --> 00:25:57,703
Stop it!

350
00:26:02,395 --> 00:26:04,330
Joyce, Joyce!

351
00:26:04,330 --> 00:26:06,499
Give it to me!

352
00:26:06,499 --> 00:26:08,567
Joyce!

353
00:26:09,469 --> 00:26:11,930
- Joyce!
- Help Joyce, Mom!

354
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:16,392
- Joyce!
- Try to move, Ramon.

355
00:26:16,392 --> 00:26:18,177
Liam, I'll take care of this!

356
00:26:18,177 --> 00:26:20,246
Dad! Dad!

357
00:26:25,352 --> 00:26:26,953
Joyce!

358
00:26:28,020 --> 00:26:29,750
- Via!
- Joyce!

359
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:31,290
Via!

360
00:26:31,290 --> 00:26:32,959
Via, that's enough!

361
00:26:32,959 --> 00:26:33,960
Via, stop.

362
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,314
- Stop it. That's enough!
- Joyce...

363
00:26:35,314 --> 00:26:36,629
Stop it.

364
00:26:36,629 --> 00:26:37,730
Liam, move.

365
00:26:37,730 --> 00:26:39,289
Stop.

366
00:26:43,302 --> 00:26:45,171
My dear...

367
00:26:45,171 --> 00:26:46,774
Joyce...

368
00:26:47,573 --> 00:26:49,008
Mom...

369
00:26:49,008 --> 00:26:51,077
What do I change?
What should I do? I don't know.

370
00:26:51,077 --> 00:26:52,525
What do I do? What do I change?

371
00:26:52,525 --> 00:26:54,180
Dear, do what is right.

372
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:56,368
Do what is right, dear.

373
00:26:57,316 --> 00:26:58,751
I will write...

374
00:26:58,751 --> 00:27:03,422
I will write it that Ramon didn't find us.

375
00:27:03,422 --> 00:27:04,824
That's how I will revise it.

376
00:27:04,824 --> 00:27:06,192
No, dear.

377
00:27:06,192 --> 00:27:09,428
Do it right.

378
00:27:09,428 --> 00:27:10,530
I'm begging you.

379
00:27:10,530 --> 00:27:15,434
Go back to when Liam
first used the typewriter.

380
00:27:15,434 --> 00:27:16,769
Dear, please.

381
00:27:16,769 --> 00:27:18,504
Do it.

382
00:27:18,504 --> 00:27:21,233
I don't want to hurt you, Liam!

383
00:27:22,799 --> 00:27:26,262
But if I need to shoot you, I will.

384
00:27:28,347 --> 00:27:32,218
Can't you see, Liam? I'm doing this for us.

385
00:27:32,218 --> 00:27:34,186
This is for us. I just want...

386
00:27:34,186 --> 00:27:38,524
I just want us to return to how we were...
The way it used to be.

387
00:27:38,524 --> 00:27:41,093
Promise... Promise, I won't hurt you.

388
00:27:41,093 --> 00:27:42,929
- I will just erase Joyce.
- Via...

389
00:27:42,929 --> 00:27:44,230
I will take her out of our lives.

390
00:27:44,230 --> 00:27:47,033
Via, that's not true love!

391
00:27:47,033 --> 00:27:48,401
What about you, Mom?

392
00:27:48,401 --> 00:27:50,970
You will disappear...

393
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:56,208
Dear, I'm okay.

394
00:27:57,209 --> 00:27:59,278
- Mom...
- I'm okay, Joyce.

395
00:27:59,278 --> 00:28:00,546
I'm okay.

396
00:28:00,546 --> 00:28:02,081
I'm ready.

397
00:28:02,081 --> 00:28:05,751
I'm happy with the time I was given to meet

398
00:28:05,751 --> 00:28:07,386
- and be with you again.
- Mom...

399
00:28:07,386 --> 00:28:08,616
No.

400
00:28:08,616 --> 00:28:10,622
Do it.

401
00:28:12,058 --> 00:28:14,599
Go on. Do what's right.

402
00:28:18,097 --> 00:28:21,867
That's not real love if you
control things with the typewriter.

403
00:28:23,336 --> 00:28:30,192
Even if there's a typewriter,
the heart will always know, Via.

404
00:28:31,309 --> 00:28:33,512
We write our own stories.

405
00:28:33,512 --> 00:28:36,478
And even though we've met...

406
00:28:37,950 --> 00:28:40,252
Joyce is the only one I love.

407
00:28:40,252 --> 00:28:42,382
Leave us be.

408
00:28:45,179 --> 00:28:46,571
Liam.

409
00:28:48,694 --> 00:28:50,796
Sorry.

410
00:28:50,796 --> 00:28:53,165
Look what you did, Joyce!

411
00:28:53,165 --> 00:28:54,467
- Liam, dear.
- Liam!

412
00:28:54,467 --> 00:28:55,868
Liam, dear.

413
00:28:55,868 --> 00:28:57,336
This is your fault!

414
00:28:57,336 --> 00:28:59,547
- Via!
- This is your fault.

415
00:28:59,547 --> 00:29:02,108
Give me the typewriter!

416
00:29:02,108 --> 00:29:05,154
Liam, dear.

417
00:29:07,092 --> 00:29:08,950
Give it to me!

418
00:29:11,884 --> 00:29:18,774
Promise me that you will be
a good husband and father.

419
00:29:19,558 --> 00:29:27,586
I am content with the chance
I had to be with you, son.

420
00:29:29,702 --> 00:29:33,267
- I love you so much.
- Mom, I love you so much.

421
00:29:33,267 --> 00:29:34,907
Miss Via, that's enough!

422
00:29:34,907 --> 00:29:35,908
Miss Via...

423
00:29:35,908 --> 00:29:37,102
Joyce!

424
00:29:37,843 --> 00:29:43,015
Before you use the typewriter,
know that your son will still die.

425
00:29:43,015 --> 00:29:45,350
He won't be able to survive the operation.

426
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,419
Give it to me.

427
00:29:46,419 --> 00:29:49,689
Liam, can't you see?

428
00:29:49,689 --> 00:29:52,158
This is all for you.

429
00:29:52,158 --> 00:29:55,327
Everything is for you, Liam.

430
00:29:55,327 --> 00:30:01,000
<i>True love means facing problems together.</i>

431
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:03,002
<i>Forgive me, Liam...</i>

432
00:30:03,002 --> 00:30:06,172
<i>If I gave up that time.</i>

433
00:30:06,172 --> 00:30:11,205
<i>I forgot why we chose
to hold each other's hands.</i>

434
00:30:11,205 --> 00:30:14,413
<i>I wish I didn't let anger
get the better of me.</i>

435
00:30:14,413 --> 00:30:17,616
<i>I wish I didn't leave you.</i>

436
00:30:17,616 --> 00:30:21,360
<i>I wish we had faced our problem together,
with Dex.</i>

437
00:30:24,805 --> 00:30:27,960
I love you so much, Joyce.

438
00:30:27,960 --> 00:30:32,161
I love you so much, too, Liam.

439
00:30:32,161 --> 00:30:35,134
I forgive you.

440
00:30:35,134 --> 00:30:38,837
Let's go back to our old life.

441
00:31:06,899 --> 00:31:08,417
Liam...

442
00:31:36,663 --> 00:31:38,872
Joyce, I'm sorry.

443
00:31:40,366 --> 00:31:41,733
I'm sorry.

444
00:31:41,733 --> 00:31:43,403
Sorry.

445
00:31:45,037 --> 00:31:48,028
Liam, forgive me too.

446
00:31:50,342 --> 00:31:54,559
Forgive me, too, for everything I said.

447
00:31:56,448 --> 00:31:58,208
I'm sorry.

448
00:32:00,820 --> 00:32:05,561
<i>I regret that we've come to this point, Liam.</i>

449
00:32:05,561 --> 00:32:10,696
<i>I wanted us to return to the time
before you used the typewriter.</i>

450
00:32:10,696 --> 00:32:13,497
<i>Because I would stop you
from using the typewriter,</i>

451
00:32:13,497 --> 00:32:16,800
<i>and you wouldn't know its power.</i>

452
00:32:17,738 --> 00:32:21,807
<i>I wanted to be your ally.</i>

453
00:32:21,807 --> 00:32:26,097
<i>I wanted to be by your side
while we deal with the challenges.</i>

454
00:32:27,172 --> 00:32:30,541
<i>I love you so much, Liam.</i>

455
00:32:34,664 --> 00:32:36,371
Liam...

456
00:32:41,221 --> 00:32:43,275
Dex is gone.

457
00:32:47,867 --> 00:32:50,669
Our son is gone.

458
00:32:52,671 --> 00:32:54,453
No, Joyce.

459
00:32:55,884 --> 00:32:57,243
Joyce, no.

460
00:32:57,243 --> 00:32:59,578
No, no...

461
00:32:59,578 --> 00:33:05,183
No, no, no.

462
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:08,187
No!

463
00:33:08,187 --> 00:33:10,756
No, Joyce...

464
00:33:10,756 --> 00:33:13,343
No, Joyce.

465
00:33:13,343 --> 00:33:16,362
Joyce, no!

466
00:33:16,362 --> 00:33:19,624
Joyce...

467
00:33:20,532 --> 00:33:23,141
<i>I chose to come back with you</i>

468
00:33:23,141 --> 00:33:25,874
<i>even though I know the price to pay.</i>

469
00:33:28,274 --> 00:33:31,543
<i>We will fight together, Liam.</i>

470
00:33:31,543 --> 00:33:34,475
Dex, Dex...

471
00:33:34,475 --> 00:33:37,049
No.

472
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:49,265
[Dexter T. Herrera]

473
00:33:49,265 --> 00:33:52,304
Happy 40th day, my son.

474
00:34:09,234 --> 00:34:12,210
[Dexter T. Herrera]
[April 3, 2015 - March 22, 2022]

475
00:34:18,924 --> 00:34:22,413
It's my fault that this happened to our son.

476
00:34:28,434 --> 00:34:31,438
Hon, no.

477
00:34:36,031 --> 00:34:37,828
Joyce...

478
00:34:41,513 --> 00:34:47,711
I want your suffering to end.

479
00:34:58,834 --> 00:35:01,172
What do you mean?

480
00:35:02,810 --> 00:35:06,760
I gave you...

481
00:35:06,760 --> 00:35:12,478
a miserable life.

482
00:35:17,547 --> 00:35:20,239
I brought you this tragedy.

483
00:35:25,473 --> 00:35:31,913
I was also the reason for the hardships

484
00:35:31,913 --> 00:35:34,770
that you went through.

485
00:35:36,515 --> 00:35:38,473
You and my son.

486
00:35:42,876 --> 00:35:45,098
I'm a worthless father.

487
00:35:48,982 --> 00:35:52,452
I'm a worthless husband, Joyce.

488
00:35:52,452 --> 00:35:54,488
Hon, no...

489
00:35:54,488 --> 00:35:57,174
Hon, don't say that.

490
00:35:59,226 --> 00:36:02,919
We'll get through this together.

491
00:36:04,298 --> 00:36:06,411
The two of us.

492
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:10,737
Liam, forgive me.

493
00:36:10,737 --> 00:36:14,972
Forgive me if I made you feel
you're not enough. That's wrong.

494
00:36:15,630 --> 00:36:21,558
Honestly, I was the one who wasn't content.

495
00:36:23,221 --> 00:36:25,839
I know it in my heart.

496
00:36:29,159 --> 00:36:31,237
Hon, please.

497
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:35,034
You're right, Joyce.

498
00:36:41,435 --> 00:36:47,933
All this happened because I'm weak...

499
00:36:50,510 --> 00:36:53,833
Because I made mistakes.

500
00:36:57,284 --> 00:37:00,856
You don't deserve a husband like me.

501
00:37:02,289 --> 00:37:04,957
I hope you understand...

502
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:11,131
that I'm doing this for you.

503
00:37:17,037 --> 00:37:20,035
Believe it or not...

504
00:37:21,836 --> 00:37:28,355
I only want you to be happy.

505
00:37:32,519 --> 00:37:37,697
I can't bear to see you
continue to get hurt because of me.

506
00:37:43,363 --> 00:37:46,267
Maybe I should...

507
00:37:49,967 --> 00:37:51,738
I should stay away from you.

508
00:37:51,738 --> 00:37:53,900
Liam...

509
00:37:53,900 --> 00:37:55,806
Liam.

510
00:38:06,186 --> 00:38:08,810
I'm setting you free.

511
00:38:26,540 --> 00:38:30,507
<i>Using the typewriter
has a price to pay indeed.</i>

512
00:38:31,812 --> 00:38:34,781
<i>I thought we would
get through this together...</i>

513
00:38:34,781 --> 00:38:37,951
<i>That we would hold on together.</i>

514
00:38:37,951 --> 00:38:40,987
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

515
00:38:40,987 --> 00:38:44,937
<i>Maybe this is the end of our story.</i>

516
00:39:01,717 --> 00:39:03,237
Dad...

517
00:39:08,206 --> 00:39:12,085
I can't understand...

518
00:39:12,085 --> 00:39:15,193
why this had to happen to my son.

519
00:39:17,357 --> 00:39:19,126
It hurts.

520
00:39:19,126 --> 00:39:21,142
It hurts so much.

521
00:39:24,264 --> 00:39:26,592
It hurts so much.

522
00:39:29,803 --> 00:39:31,702
It hurts so much, Dad.

523
00:39:36,494 --> 00:39:38,612
It hurts so much, Dad.

524
00:39:38,612 --> 00:39:40,900
This is all my fault.

525
00:39:44,451 --> 00:39:46,689
This is all my fault, Dad.

526
00:39:49,956 --> 00:39:52,626
<i>Mommy Tess...</i>

527
00:39:52,626 --> 00:39:55,962
<i>Mom, please forgive me.</i>

528
00:39:55,962 --> 00:39:59,775
<i>Sorry I was not able to fight.</i>

529
00:40:00,967 --> 00:40:03,870
<i>Forgive me for wasting your sacrifice...</i>

530
00:40:03,870 --> 00:40:06,839
<i>because we're no longer together.</i>

531
00:40:09,309 --> 00:40:12,145
<i>I promise you, Mom.</i>

532
00:40:12,145 --> 00:40:15,982
<i>I will wait until Liam
can finally forgive himself</i>

533
00:40:15,982 --> 00:40:18,710
<i>for what happened to our son.</i>

534
00:40:21,721 --> 00:40:24,905
<i>I'm sorry, son.</i>

535
00:40:24,905 --> 00:40:29,437
<i>I'm no God to use the typewriter
to bring you back to life.</i>

536
00:40:31,431 --> 00:40:34,108
<i>Rest in peace, Dex, my son.</i>

537
00:40:35,522 --> 00:40:38,280
<i>Your dad and I love you so much.</i>

538
00:41:31,033 --> 00:41:33,476
[Three years later]

539
00:41:56,816 --> 00:41:59,352
<i>Dex, my son...</i>

540
00:41:59,352 --> 00:42:02,321
<i>Mom's already here in Paris.</i>

541
00:42:03,143 --> 00:42:06,409
<i>I have already fulfilled my life-long dream.</i>

542
00:42:08,588 --> 00:42:13,652
<i>Too bad, your dad and I
couldn't fulfill it together.</i>

543
00:42:28,331 --> 00:42:30,181
- Mommy?
- <i>Joyce!</i>

544
00:42:30,181 --> 00:42:32,149
- Dad.
- <i>How's your vacation?</i>

545
00:42:32,149 --> 00:42:34,051
<i>It's good.</i>

546
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:38,155
Too bad I couldn't bring
the two of you with me.

547
00:42:38,155 --> 00:42:40,358
<i>Don't worry about us, dear.</i>

548
00:42:40,358 --> 00:42:42,159
<i>We're happy if you're happy.</i>

549
00:42:42,159 --> 00:42:46,409
<i>You have finally fulfilled your dream.
You really are in Paris.</i>

550
00:42:59,469 --> 00:43:03,214
<i>Joyce, sorry, I don't want to say this.</i>

551
00:43:03,214 --> 00:43:05,616
<i>I don't want to ruin your vacation, but...</i>

552
00:43:05,616 --> 00:43:09,477
<i>you have to know that...</i>

553
00:43:10,888 --> 00:43:15,961
The annulment papers that Liam filed
already arrived.

554
00:43:15,961 --> 00:43:17,763
<i>What's your plan, my dear?</i>

555
00:43:17,763 --> 00:43:20,625
<i>Are you really going to file an annulment?</i>

556
00:43:22,668 --> 00:43:25,236
<i>Did Liam already show up?</i>

557
00:43:27,758 --> 00:43:34,980
<i>The lawyers are the only ones who answer us.</i>

558
00:43:34,980 --> 00:43:38,756
I won't stop Liam...

559
00:43:40,425 --> 00:43:42,980
if that's what he wants, Mom.

560
00:43:45,460 --> 00:43:48,961
It'll be a waste, dear.

561
00:43:48,961 --> 00:43:51,530
<i>Someone's calling me.</i>

562
00:43:51,530 --> 00:43:53,632
It might be Liam.

563
00:43:53,632 --> 00:43:55,868
Mom, that's impossible.

564
00:43:55,868 --> 00:43:58,014
He won't call me.

565
00:43:58,837 --> 00:44:00,305
I'll hang up now.

566
00:44:00,305 --> 00:44:02,040
Bye, Mom. Bye, Dad.

567
00:44:02,040 --> 00:44:03,041
I love you.

568
00:44:03,041 --> 00:44:05,986
<i>I love you, dear. Enjoy it there, dear.</i>

569
00:44:09,815 --> 00:44:12,080
Miss Malvarosa?

570
00:44:20,058 --> 00:44:23,380
I am now Mrs. Baudin.

571
00:44:24,596 --> 00:44:27,723
The city of love didn't fail me.

572
00:44:27,723 --> 00:44:31,203
I have found my forever in Paris.

573
00:44:31,203 --> 00:44:35,807
I'm so happy for you, Mrs. Malvarosa.

574
00:44:37,009 --> 00:44:39,701
Mrs. Baudin.

575
00:44:41,779 --> 00:44:45,826
I am happy for what you've become, Joyce.

576
00:44:45,826 --> 00:44:47,905
Imagine.

577
00:44:47,905 --> 00:44:52,524
Who would have thought
that my most beautiful student

578
00:44:52,524 --> 00:44:57,685
is also kind-hearted?

579
00:44:58,730 --> 00:45:03,685
I've long been wanting to work
for a children's foundation.

580
00:45:05,332 --> 00:45:09,890
How is it to be Liam's wife?

581
00:45:12,277 --> 00:45:18,883
We separated after what happened to our son.

582
00:45:20,013 --> 00:45:27,034
Your lectures were correct.

583
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:31,809
There's no permanent thing in this life.

584
00:45:32,731 --> 00:45:34,700
Everything can change.

585
00:45:35,734 --> 00:45:39,911
Like the pain in here.

586
00:45:40,806 --> 00:45:44,723
It can go away eventually...

587
00:45:45,644 --> 00:45:50,449
like the change you longed for yourself

588
00:45:50,449 --> 00:45:52,985
and your loved ones.

589
00:45:52,985 --> 00:45:54,286
Who knows?

590
00:45:54,286 --> 00:45:58,372
Your situation with Liam can still change.

591
00:45:59,239 --> 00:46:01,528
It's not too late.

592
00:46:05,163 --> 00:46:09,635
Wherever life takes me,

593
00:46:09,635 --> 00:46:18,246
whatever change happens, I will accept it.

594
00:46:18,246 --> 00:46:26,551
The beauty of Paris will help you
let go of the burden you feel.

595
00:46:26,551 --> 00:46:28,233
I hope so.

596
00:46:29,077 --> 00:46:35,426
By the way, I have a Filipino friend
who gives tours here in Paris.

597
00:46:35,426 --> 00:46:39,933
It's my treat
for one of my favorite students.

598
00:46:40,632 --> 00:46:42,968
I will include your name in the list

599
00:46:42,968 --> 00:46:46,905
of those who will tour
with his agency today, okay?

600
00:46:46,905 --> 00:46:49,875
Thank you so much, ma'am.

601
00:46:49,875 --> 00:46:51,658
You're welcome.

602
00:47:15,766 --> 00:47:20,170
<i>All our happy memories...</i>

603
00:47:21,788 --> 00:47:24,176
<i>were replaced by painful ones, Liam.</i>

604
00:47:25,889 --> 00:47:32,495
<i>I hope you also slowly
get through all the bitterness.</i>

605
00:48:15,627 --> 00:48:17,218
Liam.

606
00:48:27,272 --> 00:48:31,108
For the last time,
before we bid each other goodbye,

607
00:48:31,108 --> 00:48:33,510
tell me everything you want to say.

608
00:48:33,510 --> 00:48:35,241
Get straight to the point.

609
00:48:35,241 --> 00:48:38,382
When I saw you here,
I was reminded of my mistakes.

610
00:48:38,382 --> 00:48:43,983
Let's make it happy
if this is where we will separate.

611
00:48:44,701 --> 00:48:46,280
[Via dela Peña rocking at the Fashion Week
in the city of love!]

612
00:48:47,929 --> 00:48:49,742
Sorry, bro.
